  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 330 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nAny degree of relief will be short lived Sunday and Monday as\nthe upper ridge rebounds with heights likely climbing to 596dm \nMonday into Tuesday and 850 mb temperatures warming to around 25\ndegrees. This will lead to temperatures and heat indices to \nonce again climb back to near or around triple digits CWA-wide \nTuesday. \n\nA more significant shortwave moving along the Canadian border\nwill flatten the ridge Wednesday with a frontal boundary\nexpected to descend into Missouri. Better rain chances will be\nover central Missouri with decreasing coverage farther south.\nAmounts are expected to be limited to a tenth to a quarter inch. \n\nFalling heights will lead to moderating temperatures following\nthe front into next weekend.",
